From bacce38936e260feb16fbb5a480ff0b3a9061ffc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:55:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Interactive terminal chat with the H224 keyboard model (H224
 missing -> partial)

`nerva chat -i` (agents/cli/repl.py) is built on stdlib GNU readline, because
prompt_toolkit is not a pinned dependency.

Keys:
- Ctrl+C clears the draft, else stops the running turn, else arms exit; a
  second press exits.
- Alt+Enter, and Shift+Enter where the terminal sends it as its own sequence,
  adds a newline; so does a trailing backslash.
- Bracketed paste keeps a multi-line paste as one draft.
- Ctrl+X Ctrl+E and /edit open $EDITOR on a 0600 temp file.
- Ctrl+L redraws; Esc Esc kills the draft.
- Tab/Shift+Tab cycle /api/commands slash commands and @file: paths.

Also: persistent 0600 JSONL history, a queue for messages typed during a turn,
/image and /paste-image (vision turn), /switch (session switcher), and /model
(the owner's local-model picker).

Server side: new user-guarded POST /chat/interrupt cancels only turns that the
caller's own credential started (agents/core/turn_interrupts.py, keyed by the
http_actor hash). The /chat door absorbs only that cancel and answers with a
fixed reply and a turn_interrupted notice.

Route snapshots, API sweep, HUD parity machine-facing entry, Hermes
assessment, areas suite, CHANGELOG, BACKLOG, ARCHITECTURE and CLI docs are
updated. +53 tests (tests/test_h224_terminal_interaction.py).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
